(4551000, 650539, 67697, '<td valign="top">What I like about this is the candidness of the shot.  It''s like you are being allowed for this fleeting moment to take this photo.  The eyes kind of say it all here.  Lots of emotion being conveyed and that is what makes this a cool picture.</td>', 'What I like about this is the candidness of the shot.  It''s like you are being allowed for this fleeting moment to take this photo.  The eyes kind of say it all here.  Lots of emotion being conveyed and that is what makes this a cool picture.', '2008-03-09 22:51:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(4551053, 650888, 67697, '<td valign="top">He really does have a sweet face.  I wouldn''t mind seeing how this would look if you cropped off the left side and put more framing emphasis on his face.  He looks like he is either getting ready to speak or give a big kiss lol - very cute!</td>', 'He really does have a sweet face.  I wouldn''t mind seeing how this would look if you cropped off the left side and put more framing emphasis on his face.  He looks like he is either getting ready to speak or give a big kiss lol - very cute!', '2008-03-09 23:18:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(4551078, 650454, 70036, '<td valign="top"><i>Greetings from the Critique Club:</i> <br/> <br/>Very creative photo. Expression is good, exposure is good.  <br/> <br/>Composition:  this is where you could have scored better.  As your commentors have mentioned, the foreground detracts from the image.  I would remove all of the out of focus foreground and leave enough of the rug to frame his face.<br/> <br/>The image as a whole needs some sharpening.  I would start with the face and allow the focus to go towards his face by making it sharper in contrast to the out of focus background.  This will allow his face to pop a bit more and stand out.<br/> <br/>Might even desat the brown in the background a bit so it does not detract from that face.  Use of levels and brite/contrast on face only would help as well<br/> <br/>Great submission, Keep up the good work.<br/> <br/>alexzen</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club:  Very creative photo. Expression is good, exposure is good.   Composition:  this is where you could have scored better.  As your commentors have mentioned, the foreground detracts from the image.  I would remove all of the out of focus foreground and leave enough of the rug to frame his face. The image as a whole needs some sharpening.  I would start with the face and allow the focus to go towards his face by making it sharper in contrast to the out of focus background.  This will allow his face to pop a bit more and stand out. Might even desat the brown in the background a bit so it does not detract from that face.  Use of levels and brite/contrast on face only would help as well Great submission, Keep up the good work. alexzen', '2008-03-09 23:36:33.000000', NULL, 0),
